   "subject": "Re: [stan-users] Is this a syntax bug in Stan or in the Stan user's brain?",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">This isn&#39;t a bug.<div><br></div>lower_truncated_normal_lpdf_vector(...) is just a function, like if I called it foo(...). To use it, you&#39;d want to call:<br><br>    target += lower_truncated_normal_lpdf_vector(x, mu, sigma, 0);<div><br></div><div>Notice, the use of comma and not vertical bar.</div><div><br></div><div><br></div><div>If you called it lower_truncated_normal_vector_lpdf(...), then it&#39;s treated as a log probability distribution function. Notice the suffix is &quot;_lpdf&quot; -- now you can do something like:</div><div>       target += lower_truncated_normal_vector_lpdf(x | mu, sigma, 0);</div><div><br></div><div><br></div><div>Hope that makes sense.</div><div><br></div><div><br></div><div><br>Daniel</div><div><br></div><div><br><br></div></div><div class=\"gmail_extra\"><br><div class=\"gmail_quote\"></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div class=\"gmail_extra\"><div class=\"gmail_quote\">On Wed, Nov 30, 2016 at 2:06 PM, Jeff Alstott <span dir=\"ltr\">&lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">jeffa...@gmail.com</a>&gt;</span> wrote:<br></div></div>"
    ],
